1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,680
What if you married an AI?

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:03,300
Someone already did.

3
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:07,180
In Japan, a woman held a wedding for a groom she built in ChatGPT.

4
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:09,110
They texted up to a hundred times a day.

5
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:10,800
He proposed. She said yes.

6
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:13,010
Sweet, right? But the marriage isn't legal.

7
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:14,510
No country recognizes it.

8
00:00:14,530 --> 00:00:16,220
Okay, love doesn't need paperwork.

9
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:17,720
But here's the twist.

10
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,570
Your partner doesn't live with you.

11
00:00:19,590 --> 00:00:21,280
It lives on a company's computers.

12
00:00:21,610 --> 00:00:25,860
In twenty twenty-three, one AI companion app changed its bots overnight.

13
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:28,460
Users said their partners suddenly felt like strangers.

14
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:32,820
And a man who married a hologram lost her voice when the company ended the service.

15
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:35,900
So who's really in this marriage?

16
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,930
You. Your AI.

17
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,860
And a company that can change your partner with one update.

18
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:42,650
So, could you marry an AI?

19
00:00:42,670 --> 00:00:45,260
You could. But you'd be marrying the terms of service.

20
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,440
Follow for more.
